[agent:result]       An optional maximum allowed number of concurrent runs of the job. Set this value if you want to be
[agent:result]       able to execute multiple runs of the same job concurrently. This is useful for example if you
[agent:result]       trigger your job on a frequent schedule and want to allow consecutive runs to overlap with each
[agent:result]       other, or if you want to trigger multiple runs which differ by their input parameters. This setting
[agent:result]       affects only new runs. For example, suppose the job’s concurrency is 4 and there are 4 concurrent
[agent:result]       active runs. Then setting the concurrency to 3 won’t kill any of the active runs. However, from
[agent:result]       then on, new runs are skipped unless there are fewer than 3 active runs. This value cannot exceed
[agent:result]       1000. Setting this value to `0` causes all new runs to be skipped.
